# REQUIRES: python-api, hdf5, cuda
# The derivative of the energy in the tunable parameters
# (D230) in a simulation continued from a checkpoint, on the
# GPU: the checks of python-tunable-gradient-checkpoint.test.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_tunable_gradient.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide checkpoint GPU Double %t | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Double"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_tunable_gradient.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide checkpoint GPU Mixed %t | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Mixed"
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: continued from a checkpoint, the derivative and its energy equal those of the simulation that wrote it to the bit: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: a new stage from a checkpoint, the derivative and its energy equal those of the simulation that wrote it to the bit: True
# CHECK: checkpoint passed
